From: Research Team <research@example.local>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 11:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] RFC (DO NOT SUBMIT): mm: add MADV_SEMANTIC_* definitions to UAPI

/* RFC ONLY – NOT FOR SUBMISSION */

Add three new madvise hints to allow userspace to signal memory
access semantics for inference workloads. These hints allow the
kernel to make proactive reclaim decisions based on application-level
knowledge of data lifecycle.

- MADV_SEMANTIC_STREAMING (30): Low-reuse data (e.g. weights during loading).
- MADV_SEMANTIC_REUSE (31): High-priority, high-reuse data (e.g. KV cache).
- MADV_SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL (32): Short-lived buffers (e.g. intermediate tensors).

Signed-off-by: Research Team <research@example.local>
---
 include/uapi/asm-generic/mman-common.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/uapi/asm-generic/mman-common.h b/include/uapi/asm-generic/mman-common.h
index 6ce1f1ce5..b7d0a6a2a 100644
--- a/include/uapi/asm-generic/mman-common.h
+++ b/include/uapi/asm-generic/mman-common.h
@@ -79,6 +79,11 @@
 #define MADV_COLLAPSE	25		/* Synchronous hugepage collapse */
 
+/* RFC ONLY – NOT FOR SUBMISSION */
+/* Semantic hints for inference workloads */
+#define MADV_SEMANTIC_STREAMING 30
+#define MADV_SEMANTIC_REUSE     31
+#define MADV_SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL 32
+
 #define MADV_HWPOISON	100		/* poison a page after recycling it */
 #define MADV_SOFT_OFFLINE 101		/* soft offline page for testing */
 
